diff --git a/features/clear-completed.feature b/features/clear-completed.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..a5b6349
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/clear-completed.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,24 @@
+Feature: Clear completed todos
+  As a user managing tasks
+  I want to remove all completed todos at once
+  So that I can quickly tidy my list
+
+  Scenario: Clear completed removes all completed todos
+    Given the todo app is loaded with a completed todo "Buy milk" and an active todo "Walk the dog"
+    When the user clicks Clear completed
+    Then a todo "Walk the dog" appears in the list
+    And no completed todo "Buy milk" appears in the list
+
+  Scenario: Clear completed button is hidden when no completed todos exist
+    Given the todo app is loaded with an active todo "Buy milk"
+    Then the Clear completed button is hidden
+
+  Scenario: Clear completed button is visible when completed todos exist
+    Given the todo app is loaded with a completed todo "Buy milk"
+    Then the Clear completed button is visible
+
+  Scenario: Toggle-all is unchecked after clearing completed
+    Given the todo app is loaded with completed todos "Buy milk" and "Walk the dog"
+    When the user clicks Clear completed
+    Then no todos appear in the list
+    And the mark-all checkbox is unchecked
diff --git a/features/counter.feature b/features/counter.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..afa49e7
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/counter.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@
+Feature: Active todo counter
+  As a user managing tasks
+  I want to see how many active todos remain
+  So that I know my remaining workload
+
+  Scenario: Counter shows zero items when no todos exist
+    Given the todo app is loaded with no todos
+    Then the counter shows "0 items left"
+
+  Scenario: Counter shows one item for a single active todo
+    Given the todo app is loaded with a todo "Buy milk"
+    Then the counter shows "1 item left"
+
+  Scenario: Counter shows correct count with mixed states
+    Given the todo app is loaded with a completed todo "Buy milk" and an active todo "Walk the dog"
+    Then the counter shows "1 item left"
+
+  Scenario: Counter updates when a todo is toggled
+    Given the todo app is loaded with todos "Buy milk" and "Walk the dog"
+    When the user toggles the todo "Buy milk"
+    Then the counter shows "1 item left"
+
+  Scenario: Counter uses plural form for multiple items
+    Given the todo app is loaded with todos "Buy milk" and "Walk the dog"
+    Then the counter shows "2 items left"
diff --git a/features/delete.feature b/features/delete.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..03427a7
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/delete.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,15 @@
+Feature: Deleting todos
+  As a user managing tasks
+  I want to remove a todo I no longer need
+  So that my list stays relevant
+
+  Scenario: Clicking the destroy button removes a todo
+    Given the todo app is loaded with a todo "Buy milk"
+    When the user destroys the todo "Buy milk"
+    Then no todos appear in the list
+
+  Scenario: Destroying one todo leaves others intact
+    Given the todo app is loaded with todos "Buy milk" and "Walk the dog"
+    When the user destroys the todo "Buy milk"
+    Then a todo "Walk the dog" appears in the list
+    And the todo list contains 1 items
diff --git a/features/editing.feature b/features/editing.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..89d0742
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/editing.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,41 @@
+Feature: Editing todos
+  As a user managing tasks
+  I want to edit the text of a todo
+  So that I can correct or update my tasks
+
+  Scenario: Double-clicking a todo enters edit mode
+    Given the todo app is loaded with a todo "Buy milk"
+    When the user double-clicks the todo "Buy milk"
+    Then the todo "Buy milk" is in editing mode
+
+  Scenario: Pressing Enter saves the edit
+    Given the todo app is loaded with a todo "Buy milk"
+    When the user double-clicks the todo "Buy milk"
+    And the user types "Buy oat milk" and presses Enter
+    Then the todo "Buy oat milk" appears in the list
+    And the todo "Buy oat milk" is not in editing mode
+
+  Scenario: Pressing Escape discards the edit
+    Given the todo app is loaded with a todo "Buy milk"
+    When the user double-clicks the todo "Buy milk"
+    And the user types "Buy oat milk" and presses Escape
+    Then the todo "Buy milk" appears in the list
+    And the todo "Buy milk" is not in editing mode
+
+  Scenario: Blurring the input saves the edit
+    Given the todo app is loaded with a todo "Buy milk"
+    When the user double-clicks the todo "Buy milk"
+    And the user types "Buy oat milk" and blurs
+    Then the todo "Buy oat milk" appears in the list
+
+  Scenario: Editing to empty destroys the todo
+    Given the todo app is loaded with a todo "Buy milk"
+    When the user double-clicks the todo "Buy milk"
+    And the user clears the edit field and presses Enter
+    Then no todos appear in the list
+
+  Scenario: Edit input is trimmed
+    Given the todo app is loaded with a todo "Buy milk"
+    When the user double-clicks the todo "Buy milk"
+    And the user types "  Buy oat milk  " and presses Enter
+    Then the todo "Buy oat milk" appears in the list
diff --git a/features/filtering.feature b/features/filtering.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..6d65617
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/filtering.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,33 @@
+Feature: Filtering todos by route
+  As a user managing tasks
+  I want to filter my todos by status
+  So that I can focus on relevant items
+
+  Background:
+    Given the todo app is loaded with a completed todo "Buy milk" and an active todo "Walk the dog"
+
+  Scenario: All filter shows all todos
+    When the user navigates to the All filter
+    Then a todo "Buy milk" appears in the list
+    And a todo "Walk the dog" appears in the list
+    And the All filter is selected
+
+  Scenario: Active filter shows only active todos
+    When the user navigates to the Active filter
+    Then a todo "Walk the dog" appears in the list
+    And no completed todo "Buy milk" appears in the list
+    And the Active filter is selected
+
+  Scenario: Completed filter shows only completed todos
+    When the user navigates to the Completed filter
+    Then a todo "Buy milk" appears in the list
+    And no active todo "Walk the dog" appears in the list
+    And the Completed filter is selected
+
+  Scenario: Active filter is default on load
+    Then the All filter is selected
+
+  Scenario: Toggling a todo in filtered view removes it from the current filter
+    When the user navigates to the Active filter
+    And the user toggles the todo "Walk the dog"
+    Then no active todo "Walk the dog" appears in the list
diff --git a/features/persistence.feature b/features/persistence.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..0e64826
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/persistence.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,26 @@
+Feature: Persisting todos to localStorage
+  As a user managing tasks
+  I want my todos to survive a page reload
+  So that I do not lose my work
+
+  Scenario: Todos are saved to localStorage after creation
+    Given the todo app is loaded with no todos
+    When the user enters "Buy milk" as a new todo
+    Then localStorage contains a todo "Buy milk"
+
+  Scenario: Completed state is persisted
+    Given the todo app is loaded with a todo "Buy milk"
+    When the user toggles the todo "Buy milk"
+    Then localStorage contains a completed todo "Buy milk"
+
+  Scenario: Todos survive page reload
+    Given the todo app is loaded with todos "Buy milk" and "Walk the dog"
+    When the page is reloaded
+    Then a todo "Buy milk" appears in the list
+    And a todo "Walk the dog" appears in the list
+
+  Scenario: Deleted todos do not reappear after reload
+    Given the todo app is loaded with a todo "Buy milk"
+    When the user destroys the todo "Buy milk"
+    And the page is reloaded
+    Then no todos appear in the list
diff --git a/features/todos.feature b/features/todos.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..46ba37c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/todos.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,37 @@
+Feature: Todo creation and visibility
+  As a user managing tasks
+  I want to add new todos and see the app adapt
+  So that I can track what needs to be done
+
+  Scenario: Adding a todo by pressing Enter
+    Given the todo app is loaded with no todos
+    When the user enters "Buy milk" as a new todo
+    Then a todo "Buy milk" appears in the list
+    And the new todo input is empty
+    And the main section is visible
+    And the footer is visible
+
+  Scenario: Whitespace-only input is rejected
+    Given the todo app is loaded with no todos
+    When the user enters "   " as a new todo
+    Then no todos appear in the list
+    And the main section is hidden
+    And the footer is hidden
+
+  Scenario: Input is trimmed before creating
+    Given the todo app is loaded with no todos
+    When the user enters "  Buy milk  " as a new todo
+    Then a todo "Buy milk" appears in the list
+
+  Scenario: Main and footer hidden when no todos exist
+    Given the todo app is loaded with no todos
+    Then the main section is hidden
+    And the footer is hidden
+
+  Scenario: Multiple todos can be added
+    Given the todo app is loaded with no todos
+    When the user enters "Buy milk" as a new todo
+    And the user enters "Walk the dog" as a new todo
+    Then a todo "Buy milk" appears in the list
+    And a todo "Walk the dog" appears in the list
+    And the todo list contains 2 items
diff --git a/features/toggle.feature b/features/toggle.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..ddaeaf8
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/toggle.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,30 @@
+Feature: Toggle todo completion
+  As a user managing tasks
+  I want to mark todos as complete or incomplete
+  So that I can track my progress
+
+  Scenario: Clicking the checkbox marks a todo as completed
+    Given the todo app is loaded with a todo "Buy milk"
+    When the user toggles the todo "Buy milk"
+    Then the todo "Buy milk" is completed
+
+  Scenario: Clicking the checkbox again marks a todo as active
+    Given the todo app is loaded with a completed todo "Buy milk"
+    When the user toggles the todo "Buy milk"
+    Then the todo "Buy milk" is active
+
+  Scenario: Toggle-all marks all todos as completed
+    Given the todo app is loaded with todos "Buy milk" and "Walk the dog"
+    When the user toggles the mark-all checkbox on
+    Then all todos are completed
+
+  Scenario: Toggle-all reflects individual completion state
+    Given the todo app is loaded with a completed todo "Buy milk" and an active todo "Walk the dog"
+    Then the mark-all checkbox is unchecked
+    When the user toggles the todo "Walk the dog"
+    Then the mark-all checkbox is checked
+
+  Scenario: Toggle-all unchecking marks all todos as active
+    Given the todo app is loaded with completed todos "Buy milk" and "Walk the dog"
+    When the user toggles the mark-all checkbox off
+    Then all todos are active
